t":"Calibration curves"},{"text":"Accuracy"},{"text":"Precision"},{"text":"Linearity"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Practical Scenario"},{"type":"p","text":"An HPLC assay result for a finished pharmaceutical batch falls outside the specification."},{"type":"p","text":"A QC Chemist should:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Verify sample and batch identification."},{"text":"Check the instrument status and calibration."},{"text":"Review sample preparation."},{"text":"Verify reagents, standards and expiry dates."},{"text":"Check the analytical method and calculations."},{"text":"Review chromatograms and system suitability."},{"text":"Document the observation."},{"text":"Follow the approved OOS investigation procedure."},{"text":"Avoid simply repeating the test until a passing result is obtained."},{"text":"Escalate and investigate according to the laboratory quality system."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Government / Public Laboratory Route"},{"type":"p","text":"A possible pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Sc Applied Sciences / Industrial Chemistry","Laboratory Internship","QC/Laboratory Assistant or eligible technical post","QC Chemist / Scientific Assistant","Senior Scientific/Technical Role","Laboratory/Quality Leadership"]},{"type":"p","text":"Government laboratory recruitment varies significantly by organisation. Some technical/scientific posts require a specific chemistry degree, postgraduate qualification, experience, or examination, so the current recruitment notification must always be checked."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Chemistry"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Analytical Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc Industrial Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc Applied Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc Physical Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc Organic Chemistry"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Industry-oriented"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Pharmaceutical Chemistry"},{"text":"M.Sc Industrial Chemistry"},{"tex